From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:35:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] deps: Take WebRender from servo/webrender#4892, for FreeType
 on OpenHarmony

wr_glyph_rasterizer looks up FT_Get_MM_Var, FT_Set_Var_Design_Coordinates
and two more FreeType functions with dlsym everywhere but Android. On
OpenHarmony that finds the FreeType 2.13.3 of the system's Skia
(libskia_canvaskit.z.so), not the bundled 2.14.3, whose symbols are
local, and calls it on faces of the bundled one. Its base layer doesn't
know 2.14's internal return code -2, so setting the axes of the variable
system font fails, and checked-release builds panic on
`debug_assert!(succeeded(res))`: most CRASH results of the nightly
DAYU200 WPT run. servo/webrender#4892 links the functions on
OpenHarmony as on Android. All crates of the WebRender repository come
from its commit, so that there is one copy of each; drop them for the
first wr_glyph_rasterizer release with the fix.

Validation: on a DAYU200 (OpenHarmony 7.0.0.38), the same change applied to wr_glyph_rasterizer 0.70.0 removed the assertion from the 188 tests that crashed (113 in css-backgrounds and a sample of 75 from css-grid, css-text, css-flexbox, css-fonts and dom), and 184 of them then gave the Linux result; with this commit, a checked-release QuickJS build has no FT_ symbols in its dynamic symbol table and passes css-backgrounds/background-clip-002.html, which crashed before; Cargo.lock only changes the sources of the seven crates; test-tidy (cargo-deny included) passes.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent found the cause, wrote the change and ran the device tests)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 Cargo.lock | 21 +++++++--------------
 Cargo.toml | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

